From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:02:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 185/194] hjviewer: review fixes for the key bar's Backspace
 key name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VoiceOver did not read the key bar's new Backspace key as '지우기': it found
an unnamed button and, as a separate element, the text '지우기'.

KeyHelpTools.wrap (flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart) wrapped the
TextButton in Semantics(label: ...). That label stays on a container node of
its own with no actions, and the button node under it has an empty label.

The name is now the icon's semantic label (hjvNamedKeyIcon in
flutter/lib/common/hjv_semantics.dart, Icon.semanticLabel), which Flutter
merges into the button: one node that is a button, has the tap and is
named '지우기' / 'Backspace'. Still no tooltip, which would take the long
press. wrap() returns the TextButton directly again; its `label` only names
an icon key.

Test: test/hjviewer_semantics_test.dart, the key among its neighbours in a
Wrap is one button node with the tap and the label.

Left alone: the top toolbar's keyboard button uses the same
Semantics-around-the-button shape (pre-existing, outside this change).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
